{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513846-lhiannan-and-witches-of-echidna-connection","id":1513846,"title":"Lhiannan and Witches of Echidna connection?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-04T01:42:18-07:00","id":1513846,"title":"Lhiannan and Witches of Echidna connection?","content":"Hello everyone!<br /> <br /> I'm intrigued by the VDA20 Warriors of Glycon and Witches of Echidna Setite bloodlines, as I am currently playing a Warrior of Glycon looking for a Witch of Echidna mentor.<br /> <br /> I had written some metaplot suggestion of how these two bloodlines were born when Set, after being Embraced / bitten by Apophis, left Egypt and travelled to Greece, Macedonia and Anatolia looking to figure out how to control the Beast. In the process he embraces a magician lover, Echidna, who helps him out with Thaumaturgy and Animalism, and a warrior son of the Greek mythical physician Asclepius, who becomes the founder of the Warriors of Glycon (though the name Glycon comes up much later and I wrote a separate story for why the bloodline changed its name into Warriors of Glycon between 2nd and 3rd century CE - before I may have called them Warriors of Typhon). After figuring out how to control the Beast, Set returns to Egypt and spawns the priest bloodline. The Beast of Set kidnapped by the Gangrel and trapped in The Noah's body is actually an animal containing a portion of Set's Beast, transferred there by Echidna through Animalism to help Set control Apophis / the Beast inside himself. Anyway, this is not relevant to the question, I digress. lol<br /> <br /> I noticed the Witches and the Lhiannan share 2 disciplines (Animalism and Presence) and a half (Thaumaturgy vs Ogham, which is different but still mystical) and have mysterious origins. They also function basically as pagan priests, with the Lhiannan being more druidic and the Witches more Graeco-Roman &quot;mystery rite in a cave&quot; ladies.<br /> Could there be a connection? How does the Gangrel hatred for the Lhiannan for a mysterious &quot;betrayal&quot; fit into this? Perhaps Echidna was another daughter of Lilith, like Ennoia, but actually had a good and loyal relationship with Set and upset the ancient Gangrel? Perhaps Echidna and the Crone (Lhiannan's founder) were mage sisters? One embraced by Set, the other by Ennoia, but the Crone betrayed Ennoia?<br /> <br /> Can the Tlacique, who are officially a setite bloodline but rumoured to be potentially a Gangrel one, be connected into all this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-04T02:12:42-07:00","id":1513851,"title":"","content":"I hadn't considered this before, but it seems reasonable. You're right that there's a lot of overlap in their Disciplines. And like you mention with the Tlacique, in this scenario the Lhiannan wouldn't even be the first bloodline that was believed to be Gangrel but turned out to be Setite.<br /> <br /> If you go with the Typhon-Set theory (that Typhon was a 3rd generation vampire, Set diablarized him to become 3rd generation, and sometimes Typhon is able to take control of Set's body) then the Lhiannan and the Witches of Echidna could have been off-shoots embraced by the Typhon portion for Set.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-04T05:49:58-07:00","id":1513865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513846-lhiannan-and-witches-of-echidna-connection?p=1513851#post1513851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hadn't considered this before, but it seems reasonable. You're right that there's a lot of overlap in their Disciplines. And like you mention with the Tlacique, in this scenario the Lhiannan wouldn't even be the first bloodline that was believed to be Gangrel but turned out to be Setite.<br /> <br /> If you go with the Typhon-Set theory (that Typhon was a 3rd generation vampire, Set diablarized him to become 3rd generation, and sometimes Typhon is able to take control of Set's body) then the Lhiannan and the Witches of Echidna could have been off-shoots embraced by the Typhon portion for Set.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Typhon-Set theory spin is quite interesting!<br /> I'm currently leaning to the idea that Set was a spirit and so was Apophis, and so was Ra and the rest of the Egyptian pantheon. Set used to fight Apophis (who is an aspect of the Wyrm) like in the myth, but one day he got bitten and became a vampire in the physical world. The Wyrm's effect, along with his being originally a spirit, turned him into some kind of shapeshifting being, at first not too controlled, Typhon, with snake, storm and canine features. Once the Beast is controlled, the shapeshifting bits go into Serpentis and Set remains a vampire with a complex agenda and complex relations to other creatures like fera and mummies. He wants to free all from the Aeons' control and show them their unlimited potential - bit like ascending for mages - while at the same time prevent the Wyrm from messing things up - which requires some control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T03:50:29-07:00","id":1514444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513846-lhiannan-and-witches-of-echidna-connection#post1513846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello everyone!<br /> Can the Tlacique, who are officially a setite bloodline but rumoured to be potentially a Gangrel one, be connected into all this?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Tlacique Vampires are certainly Ministers or Setites as per their weakness.Their affinity for Blood Magic could also be considered evidence confirming their ancestry and origin.<br /> <br /> Speaking of this, I have to mention that South America is a very interesting and unique region. The countries, nations, cities, and areas on this continent definitely have a particular and distinct variety of curious categories, groups, circumstances, events, and stories. \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T05:33:37-07:00","id":1514450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513846-lhiannan-and-witches-of-echidna-connection#post1513846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can the Tlacique, who are officially a setite bloodline but rumoured to be potentially a Gangrel one, be connected into all this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Or they just tagged along and masquerading one<br /> After all, the Vikings, Chinese, Greeks, and Italians have all reached the New World before Columbus...<br /> Some evidence suggests that the ancient Egyptians had been to the Americas as early as 1,000 BC, and for a surprising reason.<br /> German scientist Dr Svetla Balabanova was studying the mummified remains of Lady Henut Taui, a member of the ruling class, when she made a surprising discovery \u2013 the mummy contained traces of nicotine and cocaine . Disbelief in the findings led to alternative hypotheses, for example, that the tests were contaminated or the mummies were fakes, but these ideas were disproved and the mummy and the test results were found to be authentic. The results were particularly surprising considering that tobacco and coca plants, which were only found in the Americas at the time, were not exported overseas until the Victorian era in the 19 th century<br /> A number of archaeological discoveries have certainly suggested that the Egyptians were masters of the seas. In around 1477 BC, Queen Hatshepsut funded a mysterious overseas expedition to the Land of Punt , which is depicted in a relief at Deir el-Bahri (in modern day Luxor). It shows five ships, each measuring about 70 feet long, carrying 210 men and loaded with gold, trees and exotic animals which can only be found along the coast of Africa and Arabian Peninsula, indicating that the Egyptians were able to undertake fairly large scale oceanic voyages. Then, in 2011, a series of remarkable discoveries on a stretch of the Red Sea coast proved the Egyptian\u2019s seafaring abilities. Archaeologists excavating a dried-up lagoon, known as Mersa Gawasis, unearthed traces of an ancient harbour that once launched early voyages like Hatshepsut\u2019s onto the open ocean. Inside a series of man-made caves they found timber, rigging, limestone anchors, steering oars, reed mats, cedar planks, and the remains of the oldest seagoing ships ever discovered, which offers hard proof of the Egyptians\u2019 nautical roots. Further evidence of an Egyptian journey to the Americas comes from an intriguing but unverified discovery in the Marble Region of the Grand Canyon. According to the Arizona Gazette, on 5 th April, 1909, two Smithsonian-funded explorers found a variety of Egyptian-like artefacts including tablets with hieroglyphics inside caves.<br /> Even if we put these aside, WoD have a fair number of Cainites reached the Americas<br /> On - of course - is Nergal, who - after legendary Cainites from across the Middle East, Europe, Africa, and central Asia united against &quot;Shaitan&quot;. Among them were the Brujah Menele, the Malkavian known only as the Dionysian, the Ventrue Balthazar, and Setite sorcerers led directly by the Antediluvian Set himself and as the clans were unable to penetrate the defenses of Nergal's lair beneath Crete, they instead resorted to drastic measures: they caused the volcano on the nearby island of Thera to erupt, burying Knossos beneath volcanic ash and obliterating Nergal's stronghold - however, survived and &quot;walked&quot; under the sea to America (or with a dark ritual, who knows?) and became known as Huitzilopochtli\u200b<br /> He was attended by three other entities, Tezcatlipoca, Toci, and Tlaloc, which the early Sabbat conquistadors classified as vampires, but who did not clearly fit any of the established Clans.<br /> The Slumbering Giant is another good example, this vampire has been in North America longer than any other known vampire. He's the sire of Mictlantecuhtli, the legendary methuselah who slumbers in Mexico.<br /> Back to Huitzilopochtli's entourage, Tezcatlipoca could sound familar, since the Tlacique venerate Tezcatlipoca, the god of the darkness and sorcery and claim they are descendad from him<br /> Personally, I don't think tho' Tezcatlipoca was Sutekh or the Setite Antediluvian's Children... it is more likely the Tlacique are member of the Drowned Legacies<br /> Pochtli's line is questionable too; bleived to be a Cappadocian offshot, but many belive Pochtli and the Pisanob are another Drowned Legacy...<br /> Ineteresting to note (or actually, quite logical) the Tlacique are forming an alliances with the Pisanob Necromancers, left and right - wich is as I said, logical, if they are both Drowned Legacies trying to survive in the modern night<br /> Personally I prefer the later theory and treat the Tlacique as a separate group, nor Gangrel, nor Settite<br /> But ultimately both theories could work, whataver you prefer in you game; pnelty of exmaples of Cainites travelled to the Americas in ancient times and real world discoveries are supports the theory/possibility, Egyptians - thus Settites - reached the &quot;New World&quot;<br /> Really, whatever you prefer in your games<br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 06-10-2023, 08:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}